THE MAYOR OF MATARAM,
Considering : a. that violence against women and children is an act that violates the rights and dignity of women and children as human beings;
b. that the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence has not been carried out optimally;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children from Acts of Violence;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 4 of 1993 concerning the Establishment of the Second Level Regional Municipality of Mataram (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1993 Number 66, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3531);
3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);
4. Law Number 23 of 2004 Concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
5. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 12 of 2008 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);
6. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
7. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
8. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
9. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning the Implementation of Women's Protection;
10. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 Concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;
11. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Child Victims of Violence;
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for the Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;
14. Regional Regulation of the Province of West Nusa Tenggara Number 2 of 2009 concerning the Implementation of Prevention and Protection of Women and Children Victims of Acts of Violence (Regional Gazette of the Province of West Nusa Tenggara of 2009 Number 15, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of the Province of West Nusa Tenggara Number 45);
With Mutual Approval

2.1.text:
Article 25
(1) In order to achieve the objectives of implementing protection for women and children from acts of violence as referred to in Article 3, the regional government cooperates with:
a. the government;
b. the provincial government;
c. other regency/city governments; and
d. non-governmental institutions.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:
a. exchange of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of acts of violence;
c. repatriation and social reintegration; and
d. provision of evidence and witnesses, and followed up in accordance with applicable law.
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), shall be set forth in the form of a joint agreement.

CHAPTER XII
INVESTIGATION
Article 34
(1) In addition to general investigation officials, investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children in this Regional Regulation may also be conducted by civil servant investigators as referred to in the Criminal Procedure Law.
(2) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) are certain civil servant officials within the regional government appointed by authorized officials in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations (3) In carrying out investigation duties, investigation officials as referred to in paragraph (1) are authorized to:
a. receive reports or complaints from a person regarding the occurrence of criminal acts of violence against women and children;
b. take initial action at that time at the scene and conduct examination;
c. interrogate a suspect and examine the suspect's identification;
d. seize objects and/or documents;
e. take fingerprints and photograph a person;
f. summon persons to be heard and examined as suspects or witnesses;
g. bring in expert witnesses required in connection with the examination of the case;
h. terminate the investigation after receiving instruction from the General Investigator that there is insufficient evidence, or the incident does not constitute a criminal act and subsequently through the General Investigator notify this matter to the public prosecutor, suspect or their family; and/or
i. take other actions necessary for the smooth conduct of investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children, which according to law can be accounted for.
(4) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall notify the commencement of investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the public prosecutor through the investigator official of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Law.

