Article 21
(1) Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence, are as follows:
a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal aid;
d. repatriation;
e. rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medicolegal;
f. identification services; and
g. psychological services.
(2) Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the government and implemented by SKPD and UKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection; and d. mental and spiritual.
(3) In the implementation of duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (2), the regional government cooperates with government agencies, provincial government, other district/city governments, and the community.
(4) Further provisions regarding procedures for services, and handling of women and children victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2), and paragraph (3), shall be regulated by Mayor Regulation.

