Article 23
(1) Regional Government is obligated to conduct empowerment of women victims of acts of violence.
(2) Empowerment of victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by P2TP2A.
(3) In conducting empowerment of women victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the regional government shall formulate empowerment programs in the economic field, which include:
a. facilitating the needs required for entrepreneurship training for women victims of acts of violence, in order to increase knowledge, attitude, and business skills;
b. facilitating the implementation of various job training and skills training;
c. providing assistance in developing productive economic enterprises;
d. exploring cooperation with small, medium and large enterprises, as well as financial institutions to develop businesses of women victims of acts of violence;
e. endeavoring to provide capital for women victims of acts of violence; and
f. expanding access to information and promoting the products of women victims of acts of violence.
(4) In conducting empowerment of women victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the regional government may establish cooperation with job training institutions organized by the private sector.

Article 18
(1) Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 17, shall be implemented by SKPD and UKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual matters; and
g. public peace and order.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD and UKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

